  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated GBV-SRH anticipatory actions to reduce flood impact on women, girls, and third gender including pregnant women and persons with disability</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is part of the Anticipatory Action framework for floods in Bangladesh and aims to provide sexual and reproductive health (SRH) assistance and protection against Gender Based Violence (GBV) to vulnerable women and girls in the districts of Sirajganj, Gaibandha, Kurigram and, Jamalpur. This UNFPA project provides inter-agency emergency reproductive health kits, and cash assistance to vulnerable and pregnant women and girls. This project targets a total of 19,420 women and girls, including 600 people with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
